# Resume Language Variety

Repeated words make the resume read flat to ATS checkers. Diversify verbs and drop filler adjectives.

## Before editing

Scan all `experience` bullets (not just the ones you are changing) for repeated:

- Opening verbs (`Architected`, `Built`, `Developed`, `Integrated`)
- Recurring adjectives (`automated`, `dynamic`, `real-time`, `custom`)

A stem used 3+ times across the resume must be rewritten in all but one instance.

## Verb bank (prefer these over generic repeats)

Owned, shipped, migrated, launched, instrumented, routed, reconciled, scheduled, triggered, rebuilt, mentored, cut, lifted, reduced.

## Do not do this

- Do not swap `automated` with ATS-suggested filler like `mechanized` or `computerized`. Those read dated in engineering resumes.
- Do not open consecutive bullets at the same job with the same verb.
- Do not repeat the same stack list in multiple bullets (`React, Next.js, TypeScript`) if it already appears in the summary or skills.

## Examples

```
❌ ...handle localized payments and automated recurring seat-based subscription billing.
✅ ...process localized Stripe and Paystack charges and recurring seat-based billing with no manual invoicing.

❌ ...WhatsApp Business API endpoints for automated platform notifications.
✅ ...WhatsApp Business API so booking and payment events notify merchants without staff intervention.

❌ Architected ... (used as the opener on three different jobs)
✅ Mix: Migrated / Launched / Owned / Rebuilt
```
